  "count_definition": "Actual executions across O0/O2 and the recorded P/E cores, not unique inputs. Native complete-state pairs compare GPRs, flags, caches/system state, active events and RAM against independently encoded original bytes. Return checks are subsets. Earlier focused runs are not added to these totals. The 960 existing compiler/ISA cases use Unicorn; 16,480 result/fault comparisons execute real IA32 code.",
  "negative_controls": "Each ARPL profile rejects both a corrupted declared source before an intact ARPL and an inverted returned ZF after the intact ARPL. Each far-pointer profile retains its wrong-pointer transport negative control.",
  "fault_observation": "Original #GP/#PF/#AC handlers expose their vector with OUT and run to completed I/O. Original restart PCs are authenticated on both sides before normalizing only that frame PC. The shared helper excludes stale exception payload only after proving neither pending nor injected; all other event fields remain compared.",
  "test_refactoring": "KvmProtectedFaultFixture.h owns GPR lookup, completed-OUT observation and inactive exception-payload handling. The existing protected far-pointer oracle consumes the same helper and was rerun on both modes and core types.",
