  "boundaries": [
    "The code16/code32 matrix covers CPL0/CPL3, all RPL pairs, high selector bits, aliased inputs, used/unused results, arithmetic flags, read-only/missing/cross-page operands and explicit DS cache states.",
    "Non-ABI DS caches are changed only at the native instruction boundary and stop there. Successful ABI-compatible cases additionally check the compiler return/result and callee-saved registers. This is not an arbitrary segmented C ABI.",
    "Real mode, VM86, asynchronous events, device memory, all original address/segment encodings and other CPU models are not qualified here. No undefined state is invented and no missing mode is represented as a NOP.",
    "ARPL has no long-mode encoding. The full LLVM fork admits protected 16/32-bit code; NeverC retains its x86-64/AArch64 target set.",
    "Production SDK neverd-llvm-v23.0.0-r6 and gitlink 03270359c2ed8f6806533d3832a947bf883a6f69 are unchanged. Remaining i386 dispatch/scalars, real/VM86/tasks/debug, software SMM/SGX and complete CET/FRED events remain open; release/pin waits for global completion."
  ]
